From: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: boot whatever system is plugged in, never stop on a keyboard
Date: 2026-10-13

The H3 boot ROM only starts from the SD card, so U-Boot always comes from
it, but the operating system it then loads can live elsewhere. Look for it
on every USB storage device first, then on the SD card:

- A USB stick or SSD holding a system boots instead of the card's system,
  which is left untouched: a rescue path when the card's system no longer
  boots, and a way to try another system without reflashing the card.
  Up to four USB storage devices are tried, not just the first one, so a
  data stick or an empty slot of a card reader plugged in next to the
  system drive no longer hides it, behind a hub as well.
- The network targets are dropped: this U-Boot has no Ethernet driver on
  the board ("No ethernet found"), so they could never boot anything.
- When nothing is bootable, say so on the screen and start over every
  10 s instead of sitting at the prompt: plugging in a USB stick or a card
  holding a system is enough to boot it.

U-Boot reads only the serial console. On Allwinner it also read any USB
keyboard, and an inexpensive keyboard sends a key as soon as it is
detected: with one plugged in at power-on, directly or through a hub, the
autoboot countdown stopped on its own and the board sat at the U-Boot
prompt with nothing on the screen telling why. Unplugging the keyboard
then flooded the screen with USB errors. Since the keyboard was the only
reason to start USB before the countdown, preboot is now empty; USB still
starts when the boot targets are scanned.

Signed-off-by: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
---
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
@@ -191,7 +191,8 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_STORAGE
-#define BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func) func(USB, usb, 0)
+#define BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func) \
+	func(USB, usb, 0) func(USB, usb, 1) func(USB, usb, 2) func(USB, usb, 3)
 #else
 #define BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func)
 #endif
@@ -220,11 +221,9 @@
 
 #define BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES(func) \
 	func(FEL, fel, na) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_MMC(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_SCSI(func) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_PXE(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_DHCP(func)
+	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_MMC(func) \
+	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_SCSI(func)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_OLD_SUNXI_KERNEL_COMPAT
 #define BOOTCMD_SUNXI_COMPAT \
@@ -244,13 +243,8 @@
 
 #include <config_distro_bootcmd.h>
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_USB_KEYBOARD
 #define CONSOLE_STDIN_SETTINGS \
-	"stdin=serial,usbkbd\0"
-#else
-#define CONSOLE_STDIN_SETTINGS \
 	"stdin=serial\0"
-#endif
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_VIDEO
 #define CONSOLE_STDOUT_SETTINGS \
--- a/configs/smartpi1_defconfig
+++ b/configs/smartpi1_defconfig
@@ -14,3 +14,5 @@
 CONFIG_BMP_24BPP=y
 CONFIG_BMP_32BPP=y
 CONFIG_SYS_BOARD="smartpi1"
+CONFIG_PREBOOT=""
+CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="run distro_bootcmd; echo; echo No system found on USB or on the SD card. Trying again in 10 s.; sleep 10; reset"
